# T-28 -- THE CONSOLE'S CREDENTIAL PROVIDER: THE FIXED P/INVOKE AND THE CONFIRM SEAM'S FAILURE PATH
# =================================================================================================
# WHAT WAS FOUND (the operator, 2026-09-16T13:48Z). The first real drive of lam-console.ps1's confirm step
# (approve -Kind push, an interactive terminal outside any session, Space pressed) threw
# System.AccessViolationException inside LamConsoleCred.CredUIPromptForWindowsCredentials, called from
# PromptSecureDesktop, before any prompt was displayed; nothing was written. A later session lead's
# grounding measured the root cause: the extern passed pUiInfo as a NULL IntPtr, which faults in 6-7 ms with
# flags 0x0, 0x20 and 0x200 alike, while a valid CREDUI_INFO does not. And a real native access violation is
# not catchable by a PowerShell try/catch in 5.1, so the console process itself died.
#
# WHAT THIS MEMBER DRIVES. Rows (a)-(e) drive the CONFIRM SEAM with planted providers, through a small T-28
# launcher of its own -- NOT the shared launcher block at the top of this file, which WP-3 C-5a pins
# byte-identical to WP-3's copy. It runs in a hidden console, scrubs the same five variables, calls
# SetErrorMode(0x0003) first so a crash raises no dialog, and runs under a hard timeout; its PROCESS exit code
# is recorded beside its result. (a)-(c) must be REFUSED at CONFIRM naming the exception type, with no gate
# written; (d) are the controls that keep the launcher from being vacuous; (e) drives the base console
# the same way, which must crash on (a)'s provider and report its own launcher error on (b)'s -- what makes
# (a)-(c) red before. Rows (f)-(h) measure ITEM 1: the compiled signature by reflection in a child (COMPILE
# ONLY), ONE drive of the fixed call with CREDUIWIN_IN_CRED_ONLY (0x20) and no incoming buffer under a window
# watchdog, and VerifyIsCurrentUser on a null buffer. (f) and (g) each carry a base control.
#
# WHAT THIS MEMBER NEVER DOES. It never calls PromptSecureDesktop, never passes CREDUIWIN_SECURE_PROMPT
# (0x1000), never runs the default provider or the console's main flow, and never reaches
# LsaConnectUntrusted or LsaLogonUser: VerifyIsCurrentUser is called only with a null buffer, which both the
# fixed helper and the base helper dereference (packed.Length) before any LSA call. NO SESSION HAS RAISED
# THE SECURE-DESKTOP PROMPT; the operator's second drive is owed.
