Check -Id 'T-52' -Title 'THE CENSUS (BATCH-5 WP-O (b)): tools/lam/seat.py census reads every *.verdict*.yaml directly inside each folder of <root>/.mission-runtime/lam/close whose name starts with the prefix -- none under another prefix, under a folder whose name only holds it, or a folder deeper -- and classes each BY ITS BYTES, the opening of its instrument entry''s detail, whatever the copy''s name says, telling hook stop from hand tee by the name holding hand-tee-; a stop is one verdict''s bytes -- the same bytes standing in a second folder of the prefix are counted once: one row, the copy of the folder first in the order of names, its capture''s seconds summed once, the copy met again named in a line of its own and under --machine''s same_again -- while two copies of one name that differ in one byte are two, and the same bytes under a hook stop''s name in one folder and a hand tee''s in the next are ONE stop still, counted as the first copy says, a FINDING by name, its seconds left out, exit 1; it prints its head line, the seven-column table, each row whole, in the order of evaluated_at, the line HOOK STOPS REUSED <a> / FRESH <b> / NOT EVALUATED <c> -- <n> (unread <u>); HAND TEES <t>, with the tail -- also NOT RUN <k> where a not-run opening stands, and SECONDS SAVED <sum> s over <k> REUSED hook stop(s): the first elapsed_seconds on the first column-0 TALLY line of each REUSED HOOK stop''s kept capture -- a second figure that line says after it, and a second such line beneath it, change nothing -- read under --root by its tail beyond the verdict''s own mission_root at the digest the verdict cites, a hand tee''s never in it, every capture of a stop whose two instrument entries are both REUSED in it, and none of a stop whose entries differ, which is counted MIXED in the tail; a kept capture that is absent there, of other bytes, without a column-0 TALLY line, or cited outside the root -- by an absolute path, or by one spelled under it that climbs out by .. -- is a FINDING by name, its stop counted and its seconds left out, exit 1; a kept capture that STANDS there at the digest cited and that a second process holds without sharing is a FINDING too, after not less than 0.8 s -- said to STAND and COULD NOT BE OPENED, never ABSENT, its cell COULD NOT BE OPENED; ? s, its stop counted and its seconds left out, exit 1 -- and is read ON DISK, EQUAL again once the holder has ended; a REUSED stop whose detail names another kept path than its one item of instrument_captures_kept is a FINDING by name, its stop counted and its seconds left out, exit 1; a file so named that is no verdict is named and counted apart; a header line and keys it does not know change nothing; --machine prints one JSON object whose lines are the printed lines; a root with no close folder is REFUSED, and so is a verdict copy a second process holds without sharing -- by name, after not less than 0.8 s, in one line that is the whole output: no table, and under --machine no JSON object; and it writes nothing -- the close tree''s listing digest is the same before and after every run' `
